Let nums be a list of 5, 7, 7, 8, 8, and 10.
Let target be 8.
Let n be 6.
Let low start at 0.
Let high be n.
Repeat while low < high:
    Let middle be (low + high) / 2.
    If item middle of nums < target:
        Set low to middle + 1.
    Otherwise:
        Set high to middle.
Let first be low.
Set low to 0.
Set high to n.
Repeat while low < high:
    Let middle be (low + high) / 2.
    If item middle of nums <= target:
        Set low to middle + 1.
    Otherwise:
        Set high to middle.
Print first.
Print low - 1.
